# Doc Sync Protocol

## Definition of Done

**A task is not complete until all impacted reference pages have been updated.**

Apply all doc updates as part of the same set of changes — in the same response, before finishing. Do not end your response until this checklist has been actioned. This ensures every diff, PR, and commit contains the feature change AND the corresponding doc update together.

**Do not rely on memory.** After every substantive change, you must run the **Mandatory closing verification** below. If you skip it, reference docs will drift.

## Living Reference Pages

These files are the **registry** of documentation that must stay aligned with the repo. When the Change-to-Doc Matrix lists a file, it is a living reference. The list below is complete — if you add a new file that other agents or humans treat as canonical layout, add it here **and** in `scripts/check_reference_docs.js`.

| File | What it documents |
|------|-------------------|
| `README.md` | Directory tree, rules table, architecture overview, Quick Start commands |
| `knowledge/llms.txt` | Repository layout, architecture, database schema, non-negotiable constraints |
| `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md` | Contributor workflow; includes pointer to this doc sync protocol |
| `requirements/features/core-system-architecture.md` | Firestore schema, programme/lesson behaviour, engineering-facing data model |
| `scripts/README.md` | Utility scripts, file formats, curriculum sync behaviour |
| `.cursor/rules/01-repo-standards.mdc` | Directory structure listing |
| `.cursor/rules/04-folder-integrity.mdc` | Mandatory file location table |
| `.cursor/rules/05-update-docs.mdc` | This protocol (matrix + verification) |
| `.cursor/rules/create-agent.mdc` | Roster of agent rule files under `functions/docs/` |

## Change-to-Doc Matrix

Consult **every row** after every change. Identify which rows apply, then update **all** listed files before finishing. Multiple rows often apply to one change (e.g. a new script also needs `package.json` script docs in README).

| If you... | Update these files |
|-----------|-------------------|
| Add, remove, or rename a **folder** | `README.md` (directory tree), `knowledge/llms.txt` (layout section), `04-folder-integrity.mdc` (file locations table), `01-repo-standards.mdc` (directory structure). If the old **name or path** appeared anywhere as an example (programme slug, doc id, lesson path), **search the repository** for that string and update hits in `README.md`, `knowledge/llms.txt`, `requirements/features/core-system-architecture.md`, `scripts/README.md`, and `docs/*.md` as appropriate. |
| Add or remove a **Cursor rule** (`.mdc`) | `README.md` (rules table in Section 1), `knowledge/llms.txt` (`.cursor/rules/` roster) |
| Add or remove a **GitHub Copilot skill** | `README.md` (skills note), `knowledge/llms.txt` (skills section) |
| Add or remove a **document template** | `README.md`, `knowledge/llms.txt` (templates section) |
| Change **Firestore collections or schema** | `knowledge/llms.txt` (architecture section), `requirements/features/core-system-architecture.md` |
| Add or change a **root `npm` script** | `README.md` (Quick Start section), `scripts/README.md`, `knowledge/llms.txt` (scripts section) |
| Change **Maker-Checker loop behaviour** | `knowledge/llms.txt` (core architecture section), `requirements/features/core-system-architecture.md` |
| Add or remove a **feature spec** | `knowledge/llms.txt` (requirements layout section) |
| Add or remove an **agent rule file** in `functions/docs/` | `knowledge/llms.txt` (functions section), `.cursor/rules/create-agent.mdc` (existing agent rule files table) |
| Add or change a **utility script** in `scripts/` | `README.md` (directory tree if the script is noteworthy), `scripts/README.md`, `knowledge/llms.txt` (scripts section) |
| Change **contributor workflow or review rules** | `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md` |
| Add or change a **CI workflow** under `.github/workflows/` (checks contributors rely on) | `README.md` (directory tree under `.github/workflows/`), `knowledge/llms.txt` (docs or scripts section if behaviour is user-facing) |

## How to Apply

1. After completing the primary task, **re-read the full matrix** (not only the first row that seems to match).
2. For every applicable row, open each listed file and update only the affected section(s) — do not rewrite unrelated sections.
3. If you renamed or removed an identifier (folder, slug, Firestore id, script name), **search the repo** for the old string and fix remaining references in living reference files and docs.
4. Run **Mandatory closing verification** before you stop.

If a reference file does not yet contain a relevant section (e.g. a new category of content), add the section rather than skipping it.

## Mandatory closing verification

Do **all** of the following before marking the task complete:

1. **Matrix pass:** List (mentally or in the PR description) which matrix rows applied to this change and confirm each listed file was opened or consciously unchanged.
2. **Rename pass:** If anything was renamed or removed, confirm you searched for the **old** name/path/slug and updated examples in living references (not only the code).
3. **Registry sanity:** Run `npm run verify-reference-docs` when a root script or `scripts/` file changed, or when in doubt — it confirms living reference **paths** still exist (see `scripts/check_reference_docs.js`).
4. **Copilot parity:** If you edited this `.mdc` matrix or living-reference table, update `.github/skills/update-docs/SKILL.md` so it still points at this file as canonical (do not let the skill drift into a second full copy of the matrix).

## Canonical copy for other tools

The GitHub Copilot skill **update-docs** mirrors this protocol. **Single source of truth:** this file (`.cursor/rules/05-update-docs.mdc`). The skill should instruct readers to open this file for the full matrix — avoid maintaining a duplicate matrix in `SKILL.md`.
